Test rg46: %% before a name that is not a directive
// %% and a name that is no directive is refused by name, not left to the
// grammar, so the diagnostic names the misspelled directive.
// Without that check,
// %%optimizer would lex as %%optimize followed by the name r, a
// syntax error that says nothing about the spelling.
100/
    %%optimizer
    hlt
stop
